„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›How is it that ye do not understand that I spake it not to you concerning bread, that ye should beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆThen understood they how that he bade them not beware of the leaven of bread, but of the doctrine of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWhen Jesus came into the coasts of CÃ¦sarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying, Whom do men say that I the Son of man am?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAnd they said, Some say that thou art John the Baptist: some, Elias; and others, Jeremias, or one of the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.He saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd Simon Peter answered and said, Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Jesus answered and said unto him, Blessed art thou, Simon Bar-jona: for flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXThen charged he his disciples that they should tell no man that he was Jesus the Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖFrom that time forth began Jesus to shew unto his disciples, how that he must go unto Jerusalem, and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and be raised again the third day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmThen Peter took him, and began to rebuke him, saying, Be it far from thee, Lord: this shall not be unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§But he turned, and said unto Peter, Get thee behind me, Satan: thou art an offence unto me: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but those that be of men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkFor whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„For the Son of man shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he shall reward every man according to his works.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Verily I say unto you, There be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of man coming in his kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse